[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:One Good Turn Deserves Another]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:10.82]Who paid for Tony's dinner? | 谁为托尼付了饭钱？
[00:14.36]I was having dinner at a restaurant when Tony Steele came in. | 我正在一家饭馆吃饭，托尼·斯蒂尔走了进来。
[00:19.90]Tony worked in a lawyer's office years ago, | 托尼曾在一家律师事务所工作，
[00:23.42]but he is now working at a bank. | 但现在正在一家银行上班。
[00:27.04]He gets a good salary, | 他的薪水很高，
[00:29.43]but he always borrows money from his friends and never pays it back. | 但他总是向朋友借钱，并且从来不还。
[00:35.61]Tony saw me and came and sat at the same table. | 托尼看见了我，就走过来和我坐到同一张桌子上。
[00:39.94]He has never borrowed money from me. | 他从未向我借过钱。
[00:43.19]While he was eating, I asked him to lend me twenty pounds. | 当他吃饭时，我提出向他借20英镑。
[00:48.33]To my surprise, he gave me the money immediately. | 令我惊奇的是，他立刻把钱给了我。
[00:53.78]'I have never borrowed any money from you,' | “我还从未向你借过钱，”
[00:56.77]Tony said, 'so now you can pay for my dinner!' | 托尼说道，“所以现在你可以替我付饭钱了！”
